  "body": "# Desktop Pet v0.4.0 release notes\n\n## Independent core distribution\n\nDesktop Pet is the shared native macOS app; Herdr and Tern are optional, independently owned adapters and thin integration consumers.\n\n- Immutable core source: `e3e5cb6eb7dbeae93ac7aa71321b6a1e78c78817` (`v0.4.0`).\n- Apple Silicon, macOS 13+; ad-hoc signed, not Developer ID signed or notarized.\n- App/helper contract: protocol **4**, observation capability **2**, integration API **1**.\n- App-only archive SHA-256: `1dd9d63420f577437498edf66fbe02ee0a6faf3fbadce101a8952b027e72c7e0`.\n- Six assets: app archive, archive checksum, `SHA256SUMS`, separate signed deployed-byte rig provenance, pinned bootstrap installer and installer checksum.\n\n## Observed verification\n\nThe clean independent clone built with reads denied to all three original repositories. TypeScript, 62 Bun tests, complete neutral Rust workspace gates, arm64/system-only helper checks, strict signatures and the complete 68-file deployed hash closure passed. The same tagged native archive separately passed real Rubelia validation and symlink-routed pack export in a disposable logged-in macOS VM.\n\nThe GitHub release run passed its workspace/build/package gates but its final pack probe rejected a scratch path traversing the `/var` symlink. Profile safety was not weakened: the exact tagged local archive passed that probe using physical absolute paths. These six assets are the independently verified same-tag build, not relabeled CI artifacts; the tag has not moved.\n\n## Integration and migration boundary\n\nNeutral formula publication, thin Herdr/Tern consumer publication, the bounded legacy bridge and public consumer acceptance are separate cutover steps, tracked in the [current release evidence](https://github.com/hanbong5938/desktop-pet/blob/main/docs/releases/v0.4.0.md). Publishing the core does not claim that every host or migration acceptance has completed.\n\nLegacy v0.3.6 and beta tags/assets remain frozen. Legacy users require the genuine protocol3 bridge before a separately consented protocol4 migration; no normal discovery alias or instant neutral exec substitutes for that bridge. Profiles, user source changes and retained update evidence are not moved or merged. Unknown manager outcomes must not be replayed, and user Stop forbids automatic migration/rollback restart.\n\nActual Tern sign-in/keychain and OMP model prerequisites prevented real two-host prompt/transcript/reconnect acceptance. No credentials, account, provider, receipt or transcript was fabricated. Current Wiki publication is separately gated on corrected rendering and an initialized writable Wiki.\n"
